  "notes": "step-format uses value and style (numeric, uppercaseLetter, lowercaseLetter, uppercaseRoman, lowercaseRoman; either spelling, case-insensitive) and returns the decided display label: bijective spreadsheet-style letters (1=A, 26=Z, 27=AA, 52=AZ, 703=AAA), greedy subtractive Roman with no cap (3999=MMMCMXCIX, 4000=MMMM), and non-positive values rendered as plain decimal digits in every style. step-allocation uses highest (the highest non-retired step value, default 0), start (the explicit starting value, default 1, clamped to 1..10) and reset (default false) and returns the decided next allocated value: max(highest + 1, start) when reset is false, or start when reset is true, because reset retires the existing sequence so existing steps keep their labels while only future allocation restarts. Decided by EA-009-STEP-STYLES-2026-11-20 (ShareX StepTypeFormatter; Snagit Restart sequence), expected values come from that decision.",
